(Net PnL: **$1320.01**, 13 trades) is also positive. These days align with your higher probability for profit.\\n    *   *Action:* Allocate more focus and capital to these weekdays. Be mentally prepared for your best performance on these days.\\n*   **Instrument Flexibility:** Both **GBPUSD** (Net PnL: **$4504.00**) and **EURUSD** (Net PnL: **$3403.01**) have shown overall profitability. Continue to trade both, but be mindful of the specific directional warnings below.\\n    *   *Action:* You have a balanced edge on these pairs, continue to apply your strategy to both, but strictly follow the ''Red Light'' rules.\\n\\n### Weaknesses-Limiting Entry Rules (Your Red Lights)\\n\\nThese are the conditions where your data consistently shows losses. You MUST avoid these entirely or severely restrict engagement.\\n\\n*   **ABSOLUTE BAN - Hour 15:00-15:59:** **DO NOT** initiate any trades between **15:00-15:59**. This hour is a confirmed money sink (Overall PnL: **$-576.00**, detailed analysis showed **$-247.25** from 6 trades in the user-provided data, with a 33.3% win rate and particularly disastrous GBPUSD buys).\\n    *   *Action:* Log off your trading platform, take a break, or engage in non-trading activities during this hour. There is no edge here.\\n*   **ABSOLUTE BAN - Weekdays:** **DO NOT** initiate any trades on **Friday** (Net PnL: **$-427.75**, 7 trades) or **Wednesday** (Net PnL: **$-160.00**, 1 trade). Your data clearly shows these days are unprofitable.\\n    *   *Action:* Treat these days as non-trading days. Use them for review, backtesting, or personal time.\\n*   **SPECIFIC INSTRUMENT/DIRECTION BAN - GBPUSD Buys in 15:00-15:59:** While the hour is already banned, for emphasis: Under **NO circumstances** initiate ''buy'' trades on GBPUSD between 15:00-15:59. Every single ''buy'' trade on GBPUSD in this specific window has been a loser ($-482.00 cumulative loss over 4 trades, 0% win rate).\\n    *   *Action:* This reinforces the 15:00-15:59 ban. This specific setup is a proven disaster for you.\\n\\n### Additional Brutally Honest Recommendations & Rules\\n\\nThese rules are designed to further enhance your discipline and protect your capital, based on common pitfalls and best practices:\\n\\n*   **Implement a strict daily stop-loss:** If you lose 3% of your trading capital or exceed $500 (adjust this dollar amount based on your capital) in a single trading day, immediately close all open positions and stop trading for the remainder of the day. This prevents a spiral of losses.\\n*   **Define your maximum account drawdown:** If your total trading account value drops by 10% from its peak, take a mandatory week-long break from live trading. Use this time to re-evaluate your strategy, review your journal, and identify any systemic issues. Protect your capital at all costs.\\n*   **Limit risk per trade:** Never risk more than 1-2% of your total trading capital on any single trade. Calculate your position size based on your stop-loss distance to ensure this risk percentage is maintained. This builds on the R-multiple concept by controlling the ''R'' value.\\n*   **Adopt a ''3 Strikes'' rule:** After 3 consecutive losing trades, regardless of PnL, step away from the charts for at least 30 minutes. This breaks the emotional cycle that often leads to ''revenge trading'' or impulsive decisions.\\n*   **Protect profits with breakeven stops:** Once a trade has moved by the amount of your initial risk (e.g., the distance to your original stop loss in pips) in your favor, move your stop loss to breakeven (entry price plus commission/spread) or slightly into profit. This removes risk from a winning trade.\\n*   **Avoid overtrading:** Limit yourself to a maximum of 5-7 trades per profitable trading day/session. Quality over quantity. Don''t chase setups or feel compelled to trade if no A+ opportunity exists.\\n*   **Implement a mandatory cool-down:** After any single losing trade, take a mandatory 5-minute break. Stand up, stretch, get water. No immediate re-entry or new trade initiation. Clear your head before considering the next move.\\n*   **Maintain a rigorous trading journal:** For every trade (win or loss), record the exact reason for entry, exit, your emotional state at each point, and crucially, your adherence to this trading plan. This is your primary tool for learning, identifying subtle edges, and correcting errors.\\n*   **Stay away from high-impact news:** Unless your trading strategy is specifically designed for and proven to be profitable during news events, avoid initiating or holding trades directly into or during high-impact economic announcements (e.g., NFP, FOMC, CPI). These periods are often characterized by unpredictable volatility.\\n*   **Patience is Key:** Only take A+ setups that align perfectly with your defined rules and criteria. If there''s no clear, high-probability setup, do not trade. Waiting for the right opportunity is a skill. You have proven you can be profitable, but only under specific conditions.\\n\\n### Actionable Steps for Execution\\n\\n1.  **Pre-Market Preparation:** Review the trading calendar for the week, identifying your ''Green Light'' days and ''Red Light'' days/hours. Note any upcoming high-impact news events.\\n2.  **Strict Schedule:** Plan your trading day around your profitable hours (16:00-17:59). Be off the charts during unprofitable times and days.\\n3.  **Entry Checklist:** Before every trade, mentally (or physically) check:\\n    *   Is it a Green Light hour (16:00-17:59)?\\n    *   Is it a Green Light day (Thu, Mon, Tue)?\\n    *   Is it NOT a Red Light hour (15:00-15:59)?\\n    *   Is it NOT a Red Light day (Fri, Wed)?\\n    *   Is it NOT a GBPUSD ''buy'' in the 15:00-15:59 window?\\n    *   Does the setup have a clear R-multiple > 1.0 AND is the position size within your 1-2% risk limit?\\n    *   Have I had 3 consecutive losses today? (If yes, STOP)\\n    *   Am I trading into high-impact news? (If yes, AVOID)\\n4.  **No Exceptions:** Do not rationalize trading outside these rules. Your data has spoken; your past self has given you the blueprint for success and failure.\\n\\n### Monitoring and Review\\n\\n*   **Daily Review (End of Day):** Review all trades. Did you adhere to all rules? If not, why? What was your emotional state? Did you hit any daily limits (max loss, max trades)?\\n*   **Weekly Review:** Analyze your journal, overall PnL, and rule adherence for the week. Identify new patterns, positive or negative. Adjust your plan *only* based on significant, consistent data, not emotions.\\n\\nThis plan provides a comprehensive framework based on your unique trading fingerprint. Stick to it rigorously, and expect your performance to improve significantly by eliminating proven negative edges and focusing on areas of strength.",\u000a    "chartData": null,\u000a    "suggestedQuestions": [\u000a        "How can I effectively monitor my emotional state during trading to ensure I''m adhering to the ''cool-down'' and ''3 strikes'' rules?",\u000a        "What metrics should I specifically focus on in my trading journal to identify subtle new edges or deviations from this plan?",\u000a        "Can you suggest a strategy for gradually increasing my position size or capital commitment once I consistently adhere to this plan and demonstrate improved profitability?"\u000a    ]\u000a}\u000a```'),7,'2025-09-19 06:48:56','2025-09-19 06:48:56');
CREATE TABLE predictions (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    file_id TEXT NOT NULL,
    trade_setup TEXT NOT NULL, -- JSON string containing trade setup details
    success_probability REAL NOT NULL, -- 0-1 probability of success
    risk_level TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (risk_level IN ('low', 'medium', 'high')),
    expected_return REAL,
    suggested_position_size REAL,
    confidence_score REAL NOT NULL, -- 0-1 confidence in prediction
    reasoning TEXT, -- AI reasoning for the prediction
    market_conditions TEXT, -- JSON string with market context
    prediction_date DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    created_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    updated_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    FOREIGN KEY (file_id) REFERENCES files(id) ON DELETE CASCADE
);
INSERT INTO sqlite_sequence VALUES('analysis_results',9);
INSERT INTO sqlite_sequence VALUES('chat_messages',24);
CREATE TRIGGER update_files_timestamp 
    AFTER UPDATE ON files
    BEGIN
        UPDATE files SET updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE id = NEW.id;
    END;
CREATE TRIGGER update_analysis_results_timestamp 
    AFTER UPDATE ON analysis_results
    BEGIN
        UPDATE analysis_results SET updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE id = NEW.id;
    END;
CREATE TRIGGER update_file_last_accessed 
    AFTER INSERT ON analysis_results
    BEGIN
        UPDATE files SET last_accessed = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE id = NEW.file_id;
    END;
CREATE TRIGGER update_predictions_timestamp 
    AFTER UPDATE ON predictions
    BEGIN
        UPDATE predictions SET updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP WHERE id = NEW.id;
    END;
CREATE INDEX idx_files_upload_date ON files(upload_date);
CREATE INDEX idx_files_last_accessed ON files(last_accessed);
CREATE INDEX idx_analysis_results_file_id ON analysis_results(file_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_analysis_results_date ON analysis_results(analysis_date);
CREATE INDEX idx_chat_messages_file_id ON chat_messages(file_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_chat_messages_order ON chat_messages(file_id, message_order);
CREATE INDEX idx_chat_messages_timestamp ON chat_messages(timestamp);
CREATE INDEX idx_predictions_file_id ON predictions(file_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_predictions_date ON predictions(prediction_date);
CREATE INDEX idx_predictions_success_prob ON predictions(success_probability);
COMMIT;
